prs.body:
Fixes #366 

Creates a module and endpoint within the tagger API and modifies some deployment settings to allow us to automatically untag all but the 40 newest deployed simulation API versions, including at least 1 tag each for the UK and US as a backstop in case the tagger API doesn't correctly migrate version tags to the newest deployed version. This should allow these older versions to automatically spin down to 0 running instances, saving GCP resources. 40 versions was chosen to begin with; in a future PR, I intend to cut this down to 5, but wanted to confirm that this code is working correctly by choosing a number smaller than what we currently have deployed (around 49), but large enough to provide a window of error.

@PolicyEngine provide more details on how this PR does what it aims to, how it's tested, etc.

Fixes #2989 

Should be merged alongside a corresponding front-end PR in app v2 (not yet created)

@PolicyEngine write up a description of this PR

